# Scope and diff discipline

Before editing: name the requested behaviour. Do not modify unrelated payment/chat/UI “while here.” Avoid broad refactors unless technically required.

## After edits, inspect the full git diff

Categorize every file:

- REQUESTED IMPLEMENTATION
- REQUIRED SUPPORTING CHANGE
- TESTING
- DOCUMENTATION/TOOLING
- UNRELATED

No unexplained UNRELATED behavioural changes. If an unrelated change is required, report it explicitly.

Payment-system tasks: do not silently alter 2% fee, 3-active cap, Direct Destination Charges, Protected transfers, procurement, 12h inspection, Connect destination ownership, or soft-poll interval unless the task requires it — then STOP and report.

Tooling tasks must not change application UI, API, payment logic, schema, or Stripe code. If a regression suite finds an app bug during a tooling task: **report it, do not fix it in that task**.
